(5580357, 806866, 48820, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Marjo:</b></div><hr/><i> I agree with the previous comments, nice colors and lighting.<br/>I rated this a 7. I think the comp may have hurt the score.<br/>It <i>is</i> very interesting, but not quite balanced enough, imho.<br/>I think the rocks overpower the image...just a hint at the bottom would be enough to anchor the image. I tried a different crop (it''s a little tighter than what I wanted...<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=808380" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/5000-9999/8367/120/808380.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/5000-9999/8367/120/808380.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/5000-9999/8367/120/808380.jpg"/></a>. and it''s just cut and pasted onto a black background. I lost the beautiful lighting on the right side by doing that, but I hope you get the idea. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you too everyone for taking the time to add your comments.<br/> <br/>HarryY...  Yeah I figured I had nailed the lighting.  I just wish it had lasted longer for a better composition.<br/>bje2000...  A 10!!!  You are a wonderful person.<br/>KarenNfld...  Thank you.  I''ll try harder next time.<br/>GregoryB...  Thank you a bunch.<br/> <br/>Marjo,<br/> <br/>  Thank you for the detailed analysis.  The crop you did looks great, but like you said the sunlight and shadow on the right are gone.  I was torn on this composition and it was taken with 3 or 4 hours before deadline.  It is an HDR and while I had many compositions I liked better, this was the only set that had the good light and shadows.  The tool configuration is what I hated.  I changed it right after this capture but it was too late and the light beam never plowed though again.  (I did momentarily consider chopping down a tree) <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-07-20 10:38:31.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Marjo: I agree with the previous comments, nice colors and lighting.I rated this a 7. I think the comp may have hurt the score.It is very interesting, but not quite balanced enough, imho.I think the rocks overpower the image...just a hint at the bottom would be enough to anchor the image. I tried a different crop (it''s a little tighter than what I wanted.... and it''s just cut and pasted onto a black background. I lost the beautiful lighting on the right side by doing that, but I hope you get the idea.   Thank you too everyone for taking the time to add your comments. HarryY...  Yeah I figured I had nailed the lighting.  I just wish it had lasted longer for a better composition.bje2000...  A 10!!!  You are a wonderful person.KarenNfld...  Thank you.  I''ll try harder next time.GregoryB...  Thank you a bunch. Marjo,   Thank you for the detailed analysis.  The crop you did looks great, but like you said the sunlight and shadow on the right are gone.  I was torn on this composition and it was taken with 3 or 4 hours before deadline.  It is an HDR and while I had many compositions I liked better, this was the only set that had the good light and shadows.  The tool configuration is what I hated.  I changed it right after this capture but it was too late and the light beam never plowed though again.  (I did momentarily consider chopping down a tree) ', '2009-07-20 11:32:59.000000', '2009-07-20 11:38:31.000000', 0),
