(5583706, 806864, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Compositionally, I really like this shot.  You "fill the frame" but still leave a bit of black in one corner and this seems to balance the shot very well.  I also like that you chose to photograph the back of the flower.  The only teeny tiny nitpick I would have is that I think the shot would have a bit more dynamics if it were tilted ever so slightly to the right so that the stem was more in the corner.  However, please realize that this is probably just a personal bias of mine as I really like tilting shots. :)<br/> <br/>Technically, you have nailed the exposure, focus, etc.  The lighting really accentuates the details, and the flower really does look like a miniature sun.<br/> <br/>Overall, very well done and congrats on your top10!<br/> <br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Compositionally, I really like this shot.  You "fill the frame" but still leave a bit of black in one corner and this seems to balance the shot very well.  I also like that you chose to photograph the back of the flower.  The only teeny tiny nitpick I would have is that I think the shot would have a bit more dynamics if it were tilted ever so slightly to the right so that the stem was more in the corner.  However, please realize that this is probably just a personal bias of mine as I really like tilting shots. :) Technically, you have nailed the exposure, focus, etc.  The lighting really accentuates the details, and the flower really does look like a miniature sun. Overall, very well done and congrats on your top10! Karma', '2009-07-22 23:57:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5583731, 806882, 3724, '<td valign="top">Fabulous subject.</td>', 'Fabulous subject.', '2009-07-23 00:28:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(5583798, 806885, 62357, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/><b>First Impression:</b> A nice deviation from the regular colour images in this challenge.  Very creative and nice processing.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> For me the composition is just possibly ever so slightly too centered.  I don''t normally worry too much about that but in this case I think it may have benefited with a slight shift to the left.  But in doing that I guess your holga effect would have been a bit different.  Still, wouldn''t mind seeing a re-edited version just to compare.<br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b> I was going to say it feels a bit soft in terms of focus, but I don''t think that''s the flower itself, rather than the added grain from the Holga effect. (I''m a big user/fan of the Nik Silver Efex filters).  The one thing that bothers me a bit is I find the centre of the flower to be a bit blown out.  Again, this is possibly due to the filter and the increased contrast from the control point, but I think you are missing quite a bit of detail.<br/> <br/><b>Artistic:</b> Great choice to convert it to black and white.  <br/> <br/><b>Overall thoughts:</b>  Well, I''m glad I could read the other comments, for I had no idea that the title was a lyric from a song :)  As far as the image goes, nice attempt to step outside the box, I''m only sorry it didn''t score higher for you, but I suppose it''s always a bit risky to do something a bit different in a challenge like flowers.<br/> <br/>Hope this is helpful</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club First Impression: A nice deviation from the regular colour images in this challenge.  Very creative and nice processing. Composition: For me the composition is just possibly ever so slightly too centered.  I don''t normally worry too much about that but in this case I think it may have benefited with a slight shift to the left.  But in doing that I guess your holga effect would have been a bit different.  Still, wouldn''t mind seeing a re-edited version just to compare. Technical: I was going to say it feels a bit soft in terms of focus, but I don''t think that''s the flower itself, rather than the added grain from the Holga effect. (I''m a big user/fan of the Nik Silver Efex filters).  The one thing that bothers me a bit is I find the centre of the flower to be a bit blown out.  Again, this is possibly due to the filter and the increased contrast from the control point, but I think you are missing quite a bit of detail. Artistic: Great choice to convert it to black and white.   Overall thoughts:  Well, I''m glad I could read the other comments, for I had no idea that the title was a lyric from a song :)  As far as the image goes, nice attempt to step outside the box, I''m only sorry it didn''t score higher for you, but I suppose it''s always a bit risky to do something a bit different in a challenge like flowers. Hope this is helpful', '2009-07-23 01:59:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5583815, 806713, 39427, '<td valign="top">It is a nice shot but I think composition could be more dynamic and slightly less ''soft-focus'' to have been received better</td>', 'It is a nice shot but I think composition could be more dynamic and slightly less ''soft-focus'' to have been received better', '2009-07-23 02:22:00.000000', NULL, 0),
